foundation.question_text:
$ABCD$ is a cyclic quadrilateral, and $AC$ is a diameter.
$\angle BAC = 35^{\circ}$ and $\angle DAC = 40^{\circ}$.
Find $\angle BCA$ and $\angle DCA$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (1.732,1);
\coordinate (B) at (-1.532,1.286);
\coordinate (C) at (-1.732,-1);
\coordinate (D) at (0.684,-1.879);
\draw (A) -- (B);
\draw (B) -- (C);
\draw (C) -- (D);
\draw (D) -- (A);
\draw (A) -- (C);
\draw (O) circle (2);
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\node[right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below] at (D) {$D$};
\pic[draw, "$35^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.4cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = B--A--C};
\pic[draw, "$40^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.4cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = C--A--D};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
$ABCD$ is a cyclic quadrilateral with centre $O$, and side $CD$ is extended to $E$.
The exterior angle $\angle ADE = 75^{\circ}$.
Find the central angle $\angle AOC$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (-1.813,0.845);
\coordinate (B) at (1.286,1.532);
\coordinate (C) at (1.147,-1.638);
\coordinate (D) at (-1.532,-1.286);
\coordinate (E) at (-3.139,-1.075);
\draw (A) -- (B);
\draw (B) -- (C);
\draw (C) -- (D);
\draw (D) -- (A);
\draw (O) circle (2);
\draw (D) -- (E);
\draw (O) -- (A);
\draw (O) -- (C);
\node[above left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below left] at (D) {$D$};
\node[below] at (E) {$E$};
\pic[draw, "$75^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.4cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = A--D--E};
\pic[draw, "$x$", angle radius=0.55cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = A--O--C};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.question_text:
$AC$ is a diameter of a circle with centre $O$ and radius $10$ cm.
$BD$ is a chord perpendicular to $AC$ at $M$, with $AM = 4$ cm.
Find $BD$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (-2,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2,0);
\coordinate (B) at (-1.2,1.6);
\coordinate (D) at (-1.2,-1.6);
\coordinate (M) at (-1.2,0);
\draw (A) -- (C);
\draw (O) circle (2);
\draw (B) -- (M);
\draw (M) -- (D);
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below] at (D) {$D$};
\node[below right] at (M) {$M$};
\node[above, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] at ($(A)!0.5!(M)$) {$4\text{ cm}$};
\coordinate (Ma) at ($(M)!0.3cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (Mb) at ($(M)!0.3cm!(B)$);
\draw (Ma) -- ($(Ma)+(Mb)-(M)$) -- (Mb);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
